\f0\fs24 \cf0 Cloudflare for Human \'97 research context\
\
Purpose\
Investigate a verification layer that helps distinguish human-created or human-captured content from AI-generated or AI-manipulated content, and assess human participation in interactions. The motivation is privacy, safety and reliability.\
\
Scope\
The layer may be relevant to meetings, posts, shorts, phone calls, messages, images, audio, video, recordings and analogous interactions. These examples do not limit the project to particular platforms, Internet traffic, financial activity or communication channels. Both live interactions and existing content belong in the research scope.\
\
Research distinctions\
Content origin, partial manipulation, signed provenance, human participation, personal identity and truthfulness are separate questions. Mixed human/AI contributions and uncertain origin also belong in the investigation. CAPTCHA research is background; CAPTCHA design is not the current solution direction. Architecture and implementation choices remain undecided.\
\
Current reading collection\
research/literature-review.md is the entry point. Topic files provide concise, paraphrased summaries, publication status, limitations and reliable original links. research/documents/README.md indexes collected reading copies. The collection is intended for reading and investigation rather than a claim of universal detection or an already validated product.\
